{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>In that day. A third.</b> Most of the commentators said that שלישיה is from the root of ושלישים (Exodus 14:7), and they require a mishneh before the third. According to the peshat, it is from the root of three, for in Assyria there will be men who acknowledge HaShem, and likewise in Egypt more, and Israel will be a blessing, for Egypt will bless by them, and men from Assyria will acknowledge HaShem:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:22.571064960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}